# Nothing here is committed but source. Every artifact below is reproducible:
# run_pipeline.sh rebuilds the lot, and readme.txt documents each step.
#
# NOTE: gitignore only treats "#" as a comment at the START of a line. A
# trailing comment becomes part of the pattern and silently matches nothing.

# Fetched inputs: 1.35 GB of USGS 3DEP tiles, and the centerline GeoJSON
# from the Livermore open data portal.
dem/
streets/

# Derived data and the built deliverable
derived/
Stormdrain_map/

# Parked road-surface / street-width experiment: buffer vs osm2streets vs real
# published polygons, plus the interactive HTML maps. Kept out of the repo --
# it only somewhat worked, and its data outputs are large. See the folder itself.
street_width_experiment/

# Bay Area geojson outputs: city boundaries from TIGERweb, and the road-surface
# polygons buffered off the Overture centerlines. Both reproducible from their
# fetch scripts; the street split lives under streets/ above.
city_geojson/
street_polygons/

# Best-available road-surface layer, two tiers: real published polygons
# (fetch_real_street_polygons.py) and osm2streets-modelled ones
# (build_osm2streets_polygons.py). combine_street_polygons.py picks between them.
real_street_polygons/
osm2streets_polygons/

# osm2streets runner deps and build artifacts. The scripts are committed; the
# WASM package is npm-installed (npm install in o2s/) and not tracked.
o2s/node_modules/
o2s/o2s_mod.mjs
o2s/*.osm
o2s/*.geojson

# 1 ft OPR DEM: ~6 GB of whole tiles, plus the staged multi-block fragments
# and the per-run VRT mosaic. All reproducible from fetch_usgs_lidar.py, which
# skips what it already has. The manifest and log are the record of one run.
dem_livermore/
livermore_tiles.csv
livermore_download.log
# Same, per city: run_pipeline.sh --city <slug> writes dem_<slug>/ and
# <slug>_tiles.csv. Pleasanton alone is 12 GB over 414 tiles.
dem_*/
*_tiles.csv
*_download.log

# conda-forge environment. Only needed to mosaic collects that sit in DIFFERENT
# projections -- gdal.Warp, which has no PyPI wheel on Windows. environment.yml
# is committed and recreates it; the micromamba binary is a download.
.conda/

# Local environment
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.tilecache/

# Working copies
backup/
backup */
*.bak

# Bay Area survey -- which other cities publish inlet data, and what their
# layers carry. Kept out of the repo by choice, script included: the CSVs are
# reproducible, but only from a generator that is itself ignored, so a fresh
# clone cannot rebuild them. All three live on one machine. Track them together
# if the survey ever feeds the pipeline.
bay_area_*.csv
survey_bay_area_sources.py

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
